WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.817 --> 00:00:03.510
- "LegalEagle" is sponsored
by CuriosityStream and Nebula.

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:06.380
Get a whopping 41% off for a limited time.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:09.020
Clark is supposed to be the
good guy in this movie, right?

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:11.440
I have a pet theory that Clark Griswold

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.180
changes his name to Pierce Hawthorne

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.620
and goes into hiding after
the events of this movie.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.133
- I'll be a living god!

00:00:18.429 --> 00:00:22.199
(rock music)
(shattering)

00:00:22.199 --> 00:00:24.380
- Hey, Legal Eagles, and
welcome back to "Laws Broken"

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.950
where an attorney destroys
your favorite childhood movies

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:28.950
by showing you how illegal everything is

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.080
because everything is illegal.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.280
It's that time of year again,

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.650
the time when everyone on Twitter says

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:35.860
their favorite Christmas
movie is "Die Hard."

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.317
Well, let me settle this once and for all.

00:00:38.317 --> 00:00:40.120
- "Die Hard"

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.897
is not a Christmas movie!

00:00:43.897 --> 00:00:46.420
- "Die Hard" is a Christmas song.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:48.230
But regardless of that controversy,

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:49.870
let's all acknowledge that Chevy Chase

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.560
is the true hero of Christmas.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:52.393
Everyone watches
(whooshing)

00:00:52.393 --> 00:00:54.290
National Lampoon's "Christmas Vacation"

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:56.030
at least twice during the holiday season

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:58.750
because nothing says
Christmas like Clark Griswold.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.940
- This is Clark Griswold and his family.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:03.067
- Welcome to our home.

00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:05.080
- And we have so much empathy with Clark

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.900
having to deal with
his eccentric relatives

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.690
that we completely overlook the fact

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:12.170
that Clark has absolutely no
regard for the law whatsoever.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:14.150
Once Clark starts
degrading the neighborhood

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:17.100
with broken windows and trees
and overloaded power strips,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.160
other more serious
crimes start to pile up.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.060
In fact, Clark Griswold may even be

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.970
a crime boss in the making.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:24.860
And you thought your
family holidays were bad.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.350
So let's examine the laws broken

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:29.379
in National Lampoon's
"Christmas Vacation."

00:01:29.379 --> 00:01:33.107
(metal ladder clanking)

00:01:33.107 --> 00:01:34.950
- I hope he falls and breaks his neck.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.450
- I'm sure he'll fall,
but I don't think we're

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.110
lucky enough to have him break his neck.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:39.650
- All right, here we have our first entry

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:41.150
into the war between the Griswolds

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.840
and their yuppy neighbors,
Todd and Margo Chester.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:45.610
And you may have lived next to a Todd,

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:47.730
the uppity neighbor who thinks
that he's better than you

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:49.530
and he's above silly Christmas lights.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:51.270
He's probably the president of your HOA

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.040
ready to enforce all
the neighborhood rules

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.610
with an iron Apple pencil.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:56.840
Or maybe you've experienced
living next to a Clark.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.450
The dope who doesn't care if his lawn

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:00.740
or decorations or family
invades your space.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.070
Really, both of these guys
are very likely to have been

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:05.670
the subject of an r/AITA subreddit.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:09.120
And if you know what that
acronym means, you AITA.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:10.440
Now, Clark threatens to stick

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.110
a chainsaw up a Margo's whatever.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.020
- Where do you think you're
gonna put a tree that big?

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:17.160
- Bend over and I'll show you.
- You've got a lot of nerve

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.640
talking to me like that, Griswold.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:20.090
- I wasn't talking to you.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:21.400
- What a great family man.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.379
And a lot of the movie's
slapstick elements involve

00:02:23.379 --> 00:02:25.469
self-inflicted injuries to Clark.

00:02:25.469 --> 00:02:26.621
(staple gun banging)
- Ow!

00:02:26.621 --> 00:02:28.788
(banging)

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.280
- But he gets plenty of hits in

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:34.960
on other people and property as well.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:37.590
Clark's adventures in Christmas
decorations leads directly

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.217
to a piece of gutter going
through the neighbor's window.

00:02:40.217 --> 00:02:41.549
(glass shattering)

00:02:41.549 --> 00:02:42.640
(exploding)

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.850
You may think that was
just a harmless accident,

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.330
but Clark has no remorse for what he did.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:49.400
So let's talk about
criminal damage to property.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:50.890
Clark's mishap with the gutter is

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:52.640
the first blow against law and order.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.550
Now, this is possibly criminal damage

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.047
to property under Illinois law.

00:02:56.047 --> 00:02:57.420
And under Illinois law,

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:59.180
a person is guilty of criminal damage

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:00.013
if they perform
(whooshing)

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:00.880
any of the following acts

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.630
without the consent of the property owner.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:03.463
One,
(whooshing)

00:03:03.463 --> 00:03:04.780
damages any property of another.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:05.613
Two,
(whooshing)

00:03:05.613 --> 00:03:07.430
recklessly, by means of fire or explosive,

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:08.660
damages someone's property.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:09.493
Three,
(whooshing)

00:03:09.493 --> 00:03:10.910
knowingly starts a fire on someone's land.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:11.743
Four,
(whooshing)

00:03:11.743 --> 00:03:13.090
knowingly injures someone else's pet.

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:13.923
And five,
(whooshing)

00:03:13.923 --> 00:03:15.320
intentionally places a stink bomb

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.050
or any other offensive smelling compound

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.620
on the land or in the building of another

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.850
with the intent to interfere with its use.

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:23.130
And by the end of this movie,

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:24.740
Clark will have committed basically,

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.080
all five of these types
of criminal damage.

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:29.430
Clark pretty clearly damaged
his neighbor's house.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.340
The penalties for
criminal damage are based

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:32.960
on the dollar amount of the damage caused

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.850
or the type of property that was damaged.

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:36.130
Here, this is a broken window,

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:37.970
but he's going to have to pay for it.

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:40.090
A violation of this first subsection is

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:42.250
a Class A misdemeanor
as long as the damage

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:43.680
does not exceed $500.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.440
I don't think the damage here
exceeds 500 on the window.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:48.830
However, this is not the last offense.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.950
So let's talk about the
electrical code violations.

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:53.430
Clark doesn't stop with
accidentally vandalizing

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:54.830
Todd and Margo's house.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.580
Next, he engineers a power surge

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:58.800
that takes out the
city's entire power grid.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.690
The city has to switch to
nuclear auxiliary power.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:03.030
This may look like a simple mistake,

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:05.060
but Clark could be fined by the city

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:07.530
for his numerous probable code violations.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:10.400
For example, it's illegal
to crowd a service panel.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.800
National electrical codes
recommend that a service panel

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:14.930
have a working clearance
that is 30 inches wide,

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:17.370
three feet deep, and six
feet, eight inches high.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:18.203
And you tell me,

00:04:18.203 --> 00:04:20.070
does it look like they
met that requirement here?

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:22.550
National electrical codes
also penalize a homeowner

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:24.430
for installing too few receptacles.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.630
The purpose of this of course is

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:27.480
to reduce the use of extension cords.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.930
And when homeowners screw this up,

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:31.450
extension cords are far
more likely to start fires

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:34.500
and create a tripping hazard,
as we see plenty in this film.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.200
Just check out all of those cords.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:39.070
The Griswold home is basically
a walking fire hazard.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.760
And speaking of hazards and criminals,

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.060
once cousin Eddie comes to town,

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.980
the pace of serious crimes escalates.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:46.300
And would you believe that
Randy Quaid is actually crazier

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.460
than his onscreen
counterpart, cousin Eddie.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:50.590
2020 has been rough on us all.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.300
And here is one of the
most infamous scenes

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.540
in this entire movie.

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:54.650
- What are you looking at?

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:56.210
- [Clark] An asshole in his bathrobe

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:58.239
emptying a chemical toilet into my sewer.

00:04:58.239 --> 00:04:59.970
(motor whirring)
- Shitter was full.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:03.960
- Yes, he is emptying a chemical
toilet into a storm sewer.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:05.470
Really, all that's missing from the top

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:07.690
of this RV is a Trump 2020 flag.

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:09.750
But could cousin Eddie
perhaps be misinformed?

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:12.010
Sewage from a chemical
toilet has to go somewhere.

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:14.000
So could it actually
be legal to dump sewage

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.060
into the storm sewer?

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:16.600
Well, obviously not.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.260
Cousin Eddie violated Section 21

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:20.360
of the Illinois
Environmental Protection Act

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:22.390
which prohibits the open dumping of waste.

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:24.660
Violations under the Illinois EPA are

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:27.710
either a Class A misdemeanor
or a Class 4 felony.

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:30.900
In addition, Section 47-5 of
the Illinois Criminal Code

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:32.720
provides that dumping garbage, rubbish,

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:35.620
refuse or trash on someone else's property

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:37.670
without their consent is a misdemeanor.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.280
Local Chicago laws also make
it illegal to discharge,

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:42.927
quote, "Any noxious or
malodorous gas or substance

00:05:42.927 --> 00:05:44.830
"capable of creating a public nuisance."

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:46.990
The City of North Chicago prohibits anyone

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.150
from dumping anything into storm sewers.

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:51.210
And Winnebago County,
Illinois seems to have written

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.370
their law with cousin
Eddie specifically in mind.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:54.719
Quote, "No person shall discharge

00:05:54.719 --> 00:05:57.477
"or cause to be discharged
untreated sewage

00:05:57.477 --> 00:06:00.267
"or the contents of any privy
vault or chemical toilet

00:06:00.267 --> 00:06:02.870
"directly or indirectly to storm sewers."

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:04.750
Chicago takes this pretty seriously.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:06.050
Just ask Stefan Wohl,

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.080
the bus driver for the Dave Matthews Band.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:10.910
He pleaded guilty to emptying
the bus's septic tank

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:13.397
over the Chicago River in 2004, quote,

00:06:13.397 --> 00:06:16.187
"drenching passengers on
an architectural boat tour

00:06:16.187 --> 00:06:18.710
"with 800 pounds of human waste."

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:21.476
Yes, you heard that right, 800 pounds.

00:06:21.476 --> 00:06:22.309
- Hidy ho!

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.210
- Wohl got 18 months of probation,

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:28.330
150 hours of community
service and a $10,000 fine

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:30.160
after pleading guilty
to a misdemeanor charges

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.940
of reckless conduct and water pollution.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:33.860
He also never drove for the band again.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:34.920
Now, these are of course,

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:36.720
related to the actions of cousin Eddie,

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:38.980
who is distinct from Clark Griswold,

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:41.110
but it's possible that vicarious liability

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:43.550
could attach to Clark
in these circumstances.

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:45.950
But remember our criminal
damage to property offense?

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:48.270
Clark could be charged with
the fifth kind of offense,

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:50.250
the intentionally placing a stink bomb

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:53.220
or any other offensive
smelling compound on the land

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:54.650
or in the building of another

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:56.620
with the intent to interfere with its use.

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:59.030
The police might be able to
say that Clark knew darn well

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:00.470
what Eddie was doing to that sewer

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:01.940
and that the resulting stink interfered

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:03.120
with the entire neighborhood.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:04.540
Luckily for Eddie, there's no law

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.560
against public drunkenness in Illinois.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:09.140
So he only needs to fess
up to dumping the toilet.

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:11.290
So now, we're getting
down to Clark's baser

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:13.610
criminal instincts where
he admits writing a check

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:15.430
without sufficient funds to cover it.

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.840
- To make sure the pool goes
in as soon as the ground thaws,

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.410
I had to lay out the money in advance.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:20.910
And until this little miracle arrived,

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:22.080
I didn't have enough in my account

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.380
to cover the check I wrote.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:25.410
- Clark's excuse for
this is that he really,

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:27.670
really wanted to put a deposit
down on a swimming pool

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:29.880
and he assumed his bonus would cover it.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.810
Well, sorry, but that won't cut it

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:33.160
as a defense to check kiting.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.550
Under Illinois criminal law,
(sirens wailing)

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:36.440
writing a check when
you know you don't have

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:37.640
the funds to cover it is considered

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:39.120
financial institution fraud.

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:41.670
This is considered theft
from a financial institution.

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:43.950
And when the total amount
of that financial fraud

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:47.890
is between 301 and $10,000,
that's a Class 3 felony,

00:07:47.890 --> 00:07:49.190
which carries a possible sentence

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:54.040
of up to five years in jail
or a fine of up to $25,000.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:57.150
But then Clark goes on a further
crime spree, which again,

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:59.130
inflicts property damage
on the Chester house

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:01.225
after the tree smashes into the window.

00:08:01.225 --> 00:08:04.160
(glass shattering)

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:06.890
This is Clark's fault and
this time the damage is

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:09.340
well above the $500
threshold for a misdemeanor.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.740
The penalty for this criminal charge

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:12.710
could be a Class 4 felony in Illinois

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:15.020
when the damage to the
property exceeds $500,

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:17.150
but it doesn't exceed $10,000,

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:18.960
which is punishable by
three years in prison

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:21.130
and a fine of up to $25,000.

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:24.110
But the neighbor Margo is not
going to take this lying down.

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:26.230
And Margo is fed up with
the vandalism to her house,

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:28.760
so she decides to take the
law into her own hands.

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:30.204
- I can't just attack someone.

00:08:30.204 --> 00:08:31.830
- All right then, if you're not man enough

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:34.140
to put an end to this (beep), then I am.

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:36.010
- She tells Todd she's going to kill Clark

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:37.710
and marches over to his house.

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:40.010
Snots the dog chases after a squirrel

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:41.800
running out of the house and mauls her.

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:44.844
Now, Illinois has a strict
liability dog bite law.

00:08:44.844 --> 00:08:45.700
(whooshing)
Under the statute,

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:47.767
quote, "If a dog or other
animal without provocation,

00:08:47.767 --> 00:08:49.027
"attacks, attempts to attack,

00:08:49.027 --> 00:08:51.907
"or injures any person who is
peaceably conducting himself

00:08:51.907 --> 00:08:55.537
"or herself in any place where
he or she may lawfully be,

00:08:55.537 --> 00:08:57.747
"the owner of such dog or other animal

00:08:57.747 --> 00:08:59.730
"is liable in civil damages."

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:01.230
The law makes the owner of the dog

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:02.900
or the person controlling it liable

00:09:02.900 --> 00:09:04.530
to the injured person in tort.

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:07.790
Now, Margo could claim that
the dog was told to attack her,

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:10.430
but that's not necessary for
a strict liability offense.

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:13.250
However, on the other side,
provocation is a defense.

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:15.200
So Clark might be able
to claim that it was

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:17.465
a hideous accident caused
by a flying squirrel.

00:09:17.465 --> 00:09:18.382
- Squirrel!

00:09:19.553 --> 00:09:20.386
- Squirrel!

00:09:20.386 --> 00:09:22.210
- And Margo was in an aggressive posture.

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:24.410
Now, Margo is so pissed
off about being attacked,

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:26.490
that she quickly recovers just in time

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:28.624
to punch her husband in the face in anger.

00:09:28.624 --> 00:09:31.750
(smacking)
(banging)

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:34.090
This is basically
turning into a law school

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:36.330
towards hypothetical on steroids.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:37.430
But under Illinois law,

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.560
a person commits battery
If he or she knowingly

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:41.290
without legal justification by any means,

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:43.960
one, causes bodily harm to an individual.

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:45.420
This is a Class A misdemeanor,

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:47.870
and she probably doesn't
have any defense here.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:50.300
But luckily, Clark is
probably out of the woods

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:51.250
on this particular one.

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:54.320
But that takes us to
the darker side of Clark

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:55.960
and potential kidnapping.

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:57.970
When Clark tells the family that his boss

00:09:57.970 --> 00:09:59.190
cheated him out of a bonus,

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:00.690
he suggests kidnapping the boss

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:02.820
and having him brought to
the house for a beating.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:05.010
- I want him brought from
his happy holiday slumber

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:07.180
over there in Melody Lane with
all the other rich people.

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:09.520
And I want him brought right here

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:11.110
with a big ribbon on his head.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:13.000
- Ever the compliant co-conspirator,

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.880
Eddie kidnaps the boss, ties him up,

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.124
holds him against as will
and brings him to Clark.

00:10:17.124 --> 00:10:20.563
- Ho ho ho, Merry Christmas, Clark.

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:23.450
You about ready to do some kissin'?

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:25.260
- So by now, Clark Griswold is basically

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:27.380
the Tony Soprano of Winnebago County.

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:28.590
When the police finally arrive,

00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:31.230
Clark admits that he is the
mastermind behind the crime

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:33.230
and he ordered Eddie to kidnap the boss,

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:36.290
and like any good capo, Eddie
did just as he was told.

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:37.480
- It was my fault.

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:39.180
I lost my temper when I got my bonus.

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:41.610
And I, I guess I said a few
things I shouldn't have.

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:43.850
- But this was no simple kidnapping.

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:46.230
Aggravated kidnapping
includes taking another person

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:48.130
with the intent to collect a ransom

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:50.990
or inflicting any bodily
harm on that victim.

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:52.670
Clark wanted a bonus big enough to cover

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:55.030
the $7,500 deposit on a swimming pool.

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:58.080
This could be enough to conclude
that the boss was ransomed.

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:00.760
- I have never been treated
like this in my life.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:03.000
- I'm sorry, this is our
family's first kidnapping.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:06.000
- And aggravated kidnapping
is a Class 10 felony

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:08.440
with prison terms increasing
with the nature of the crime.

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:10.380
First defenses are
punishable by a prison term

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:13.740
of six to 30 years with an
additional 15 to 25 years,

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:15.320
depending on the severity of the crime.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.030
Second and subsequent
offenses are punishable

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:19.920
by life imprisonment and
a fine of up to $25,000

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:22.420
and restitution to the victim, whew!

00:11:22.420 --> 00:11:25.070
Clark is supposed to be the
good guy in this movie, right?

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:28.240
I have a pet theory that Clark
Griswold changes his name

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:30.040
to Pierce Hawthorne and goes into hiding

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:31.450
after the events of this movie.

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:34.210
- Pierce, you've had three flu shots.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:35.816
That's for the daycare center.

00:11:35.816 --> 00:11:37.503
- I'll be a living god!

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:40.350
- Now, the best part of this search

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:42.220
for the Griswold family Christmas tree is

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:44.480
Clark leading an expedition
through knee-high snow.

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:46.380
We may all dream of
striding through the woods

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:47.940
and cutting down a perfect Christmas tree.

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:51.260
But as avid readers of
r/treelaw can attest,

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:53.240
you have to consider the
location of the tree.

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:54.560
Is this private property?

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.850
We're clearly far away from
the tree lot at this point.

00:11:56.850 --> 00:11:58.490
And that's probably a crime.

00:11:58.490 --> 00:12:00.120
This could be trespass or conversion

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:02.230
since the Griswolds are
on someone else's land.

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:03.620
They've also violated the Illinois

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:05.110
Wrongful Tree Cutting Act.

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:07.907
Under this law, "Any party
to have intentionally cut

00:12:07.907 --> 00:12:10.427
"or knowingly caused to
be cut any timber or tree,

00:12:10.427 --> 00:12:12.897
"other than a tree or
woody plant referenced

00:12:12.897 --> 00:12:15.287
"in the Illinois Exotic Weed Act,

00:12:15.287 --> 00:12:17.137
"which he or she did not
have the legal right to cut

00:12:17.137 --> 00:12:19.937
"or cause to be cut shall
pay the owner of the timber

00:12:19.937 --> 00:12:22.850
"or tree three times its stumpage value."

00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:24.980
That's an enormous tree
that is probably worth

00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:26.240
tens of thousands of dollars.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:29.094
Clark could be on the hook for $50,000.

00:12:29.094 --> 00:12:29.927
- The tree is the symbol of the spirit

00:12:29.927 --> 00:12:32.120
of the Griswold family Christmas.

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:34.510
- Now, before we tally
up all of Clark's crimes

00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:36.150
and sentence him to a jail term,

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:38.250
let's look at all the
other dishonorable mentions

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:40.044
of minor crimes by others.

00:12:40.044 --> 00:12:42.904
(upbeat music)

